# Real server-side 301s for the policy pages, instead of the client-side
# React Router <Navigate> that used to handle these. A JS-only redirect
# means Netlify serves a 200 for /privacy etc. and the hop only happens
# after hydration - any backlinks to the old URLs don't cleanly pass their
# ranking signal through, and Google explicitly prefers a real redirect
# over a client-side one here.
/privacy  /policy/privacy  301
/terms    /policy/terms    301
/cookie   /policy/cookie   301

